  "best_start_month": "02",
  "not_modelled": [
    "the ERA5 → sub-canopy wind transfer (the campaign measures it; ≈ 2 storms cannot show it is stable)",
    "whether TARGET_HOURS suffices for the histogram's tail",
    "battery derating in cold and depth of discharge (USABLE_FRACTION = 1 — the trips are a floor)"
  ],
  "verdict": "Replayed over 1991–2020, a campaign that must collect 10 hours of ERA5 10 m wind ≥ 8.0 m/s (Beaufort 5) at the site cell takes a median 70 days from a start on the 1st of month 02 (p75 125, p90 294) — the shortest start month; the winter starts rank 02 < 12 < 03 < 01 by median, and January takes 86 (p75 142), because 14 of 30 Januaries have no Beaufort-5 hour at all: the hours come in storms (41 January storms in 30 years, 4.5 h each on average), so 10 hours are about two storms. The sheet's set (2 strain sensors at right angles and 1 tilt sensor on one receiver, 0.2126 A) runs 11.8 days on 60 Ah and 19.6 on 100 Ah, so the median campaign from month 02 costs 7 / 5 trips (60 / 100 Ah: installation, swaps, removal) and the p75 one 12 / 8. The battery days take the full rating in winter cold, so the trips are a floor; and how ERA5's open-terrain wind maps to the wind under the canopy is what the campaign measures, not what this assumes."
}
